        <workflow:AgenticOperation name="Copy A02 data into A03" status="Succeeded" captureOutput="true">
          <startedAt>2026-09-16T01:02:25</startedAt>
          <baseCommit>d380f667beefea95356609dc0be502613189e0a4</baseCommit>
          <output>All references remap correctly to A03 counterparts. The task is complete:

**A03_01_CopyData executed:**
1. **Wipe** — the live A03 data tree was already empty on disk, but `Library.bml` had stale/dangling A03 data catalog entries (from an earlier, differently-structured import) referencing nonexistent Blocks (`adata:BmlDocSet_A03`, mismatched `page:*`/`pgroup:*` names) — these were removed.
2. **Copy** — all 45 files (34→35 doc pages, 9 page groups, 1 DocSet) copied from `a02_structuring/data/` to `a03_authoring/data/`, preserving relative paths; `BmlDocSet_A02.bml` → `BmlDocSet_A03.bml`.
3. **Remap** — package URIs, xmlns aliases (`a02data`→`a03data`, `a02pgroup`→`a03pgroup`), the DocSet Block name, and sector-identity prose (`A02`/`a02`/&quot;structuring&quot; → `A03`/`a03`/&quot;authoring&quot;) were rewritten throughout. Two prose spots referenced things with no valid A03 counterpart (task names `A02_02_UpdatePageSkeletons`/`A02_03_UpdatePageGroups`, and a self-referential &quot;authored in a03 from the a02 structure&quot; sentence) — reworded rather than blindly renamed, since inventing matching fictitious A03 task names would've been wrong.
4. **Confirmed** — `blockml validate --all` shows the new A03 data tree and updated Library entries resolve cleanly; the only remaining errors are pre-existing, unrelated issues (stale A02 catalog entries in Library.bml and old archived `_meta/transform` history records) that predate this run and are out of scope (A02 is off-limits per instructions).
5. **Exported** — `Library.bml`'s `blocks` catalog now lists the 35 `page:*` pages and 9 `pgroup:*` page groups with correct A03 names (previously it listed a mismatched, dangling set).

No A02 files were touched. Changes are unstaged (`Library.bml` modified, `a03_authoring/data/` new) — let me know if you'd like this committed.</output>
          <completedAt>2026-09-16T01:08:41</completedAt>
          <task>
            <a03_task:A03_01_CopyData />
          </task>
          <changedFiles>
            <type:FilePathEntity value="packages/bmldocs/blocks/org/blockml/bml/bmldocs/Library.bml" />
            <type:FilePathEntity value="packages/bmldocs/blocks/org/blockml/bml/bmldocs/a03_authoring/data/" />
          </changedFiles>
        </workflow:AgenticOperation>
        <workflow:AgenticOperation name="Author A03 pages" status="Succeeded" captureOutput="true">
          <startedAt>2026-09-16T01:08:42</startedAt>
          <baseCommit>bf46403ce5f1445bb07a7e6da3d3670458c9924d</baseCommit>
          <output>**A03_02_AuthorPages is complete.**

All 35 A03 DocPages (the full BlockML Core handbook: Getting Started → Foundations → Type System → Members → Behaviour &amp; Values → Composition &amp; Structure → BML Format, plus the TableOfContents index) now have an authored `content` scaffold — Sections and ContentElements with `message`/`role`/`detailLevel`/`weight` and semantic (SupportingPoint/Scope/Exclusion) grounding, following the `PageExample_A03` structural template.

What was done:
- Kept every page's existing identity (title, purpose, detailLevel, pageType) and page-level semantic scaffold (authoritativeSources, scopes, readerOutcomes, learningObjectives, exclusions, supportingPoints) untouched — only added `content` as directed.
- Each concept page got ~4–5 substantive Sections plus a closing Navigation section chaining to the next page in reading order; the TableOfContents page got a Navigation tree grouped by page group; the final page (BmlNamespaces) links back to the menu instead of &quot;next.&quot;
- Content was synthesized from each page's own bound lib sources (`org.blockml.bml.documentation.*`, `core.*`, `type.*`, etc.), respecting the nine composed rules (section count, one message per element, scope/exclusion boundaries, detail-level matching, concept-before-implementation, no fragmented enumeration, no source dumps, no unrequested diagnostics).
- `CodeBlock.code` and `Paragraph.content` were deliberately left empty — that's A04's job.
- No A02 data, other sectors, or `Library.bml` were touched; the catalog export A03_01 already performed still covers all 35 pages.
- `npx blockml validate --all` shows the same 6 pre-existing error-blocks that existed before this task (stale a02 catalog entries and archived transform history) — zero new errors, warnings, or issues in any of the 35 authored files.

This work was split across one page I authored directly (TableOfContents, Introduction, CoreUseCases) and six parallel background agents covering the remaining 32 pages by page group, each independently validated clean.
</output>
          <completedAt>2026-09-16T01:26:52</completedAt>
